messages:
alice.k: FYI ProspectX demo just failed again. Their embedded webview threw a JSON parse error mid-stream and UI hung.
ben.s: Oof. What did the client log show?
dana_support: Client console: `Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected token } in JSON at position 124` and then `EventSource failed` once.
frank.i: Do we have the raw SSE payloads from the gateway for that session (px-demo-214)? @dana_support
sse-bot: [sse-session] id=px-demo-214 region=us-west-2 model=redwood-3-small start=2026-03-20T14:02:10Z
dana_support: Pasted the raw events: `data: {"chunk":"Hello, thi","part":1}
data: {"chunk":"s is a test","part":1}
data: {"chunk":"\"unfinished\"}
data: {"chunk":"Next message","part":2}` — notice third line contains an extra escaped quote that breaks assemblers.
ben.s: Hmm, server shouldn't emit mismatched escapes. Could be our encoder vs customer decoder combining boundaries incorrectly.
frank.i: What does their parser do? Many WebView implementations naively join lines and json.parse on every `data:` line. If a logical object spans multiple `data:` lines, that will fail.
alice.k: ProspectX dev said they use a tiny in-house parser that assumes each `data:` line is a valid JSON object.
dana_support: Reached out and asked for a devtools network HAR. Also checked our runtime — no 5xx, no 429. There is a proxy RESET at 14:02:33 but that was after the parse errors started.
eng_oncall: Actionable items: 1) recommend customer change parser to accumulate event payload until event terminator `\n\n` and only parse then; 2) we can emit `id:` on each SSE event to make reassembly simpler; 3) plan an SDK helper that provides robust SSE-to-json streaming parsing for WebView.
ben.s: For an immediate quick patch to share, here's a minimal tolerant parser we can DM them (JS):
```js
// accumulate data until blank line, tolerate broken fragments
let acc = '';
eventSource.onmessage = (e) => {
  acc += e.data;
  // only attempt to parse when we detect full event terminator
  const parts = acc.split('\n\n');
  for (let i = 0; i < parts.length - 1; i++) {
    const raw = parts[i].split('\n').map(l=>l.replace(/^data:\s*/,'')).join('');
    try { handle(JSON.parse(raw)); } catch(err) { console.warn('json-accumulation-err', err); }
  }
  acc = parts[parts.length-1];
};
```
frank.i: Also suggest adding small jittered keepalive pings from client so proxies don't idle-close.
dana_support: I sent the snippet and asked them to capture the full HAR. They confirmed demo paused until this was fixed.
alice.k: ProspectX asked whether this could be caused by rate limits — they saw earlier a throttled request. Is there a DC for connections?
dana_support: Verified: no rate-limit header on this session. Separate automated load test caused 429s earlier but not for demo token.
eng_oncall: I'll do a canary server change to flush event buffers promptly (set flush-after=50ms for demo tokens) and roll to 3% so demos are less likely to hit partial-emit windows. Also opening infra ticket to look at proxy idle timeouts.
ben.s: Good. We should also add a short FAQ blurb: "If you embed in WebView, please use streaming-aware JSON reassembly" and include our snippet.
dana_support: Sent follow-up with integration steps and asked for their HAR + repro steps.
alice.k: Thanks team. I'll schedule a follow-up demo tomorrow 15:00 PT and confirm once canary + parser patch are in place. :raised_hands:
